.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MOOBFS-ATTR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm moobfs-attr
.Nd read and write typed MoobFS attributes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm get Ar file name
.Nm
.Cm set Ar file name type value
.Nm
.Cm rm Ar file name
.Nm
.Cm list Ar file
.Nm
.Cm rawset Ar file name hex
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and writes the typed attributes of MoobFS, stored as extended attributes under
.Dq user.moob.
on ordinary files.
It works on a mounted MoobFS layer, where the kernel validates every write, and on a plain
directory, where the tool validates before writing.
MoobFS is an experimental research project: do not use it for data you cannot lose.
.Pp
.Ar name
is given without the
.Dq user.moob.
prefix: lowercase ASCII letters, digits, underscores and dots, at most 64 bytes, neither starting
nor ending with a dot and without two dots in a row;
.Dq format
is reserved for the tools.
A file holds at most 64 typed attributes.
.Pp
.Ar type
is one of:
.Bl -tag -width double -compact
.It Cm string
valid UTF-8 without NUL, at most 1024 bytes
.It Cm int64
signed 64-bit integer
.It Cm double
IEEE 754 binary64, not NaN
.It Cm bool
.Cm true
or
.Cm false
.It Cm time
signed nanoseconds since the epoch
.It Cm raw
up to 4096 bytes given in hexadecimal, never indexed
.El
.Pp
.Cm get
and
.Cm list
print
.Dq name<TAB>type<TAB>value ,
or
.Dq name<TAB>invalid<TAB>reason
for a value that does not decode.
.Cm rawset
writes bytes unchecked and exists for tests.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 2n -compact
.It 0
success
.It 1
a system call failed; the reason is printed
.It 2
.Cm get :
the value is invalid
.It 3
.Cm get :
no such attribute
.It 64
usage error or invalid name
.It 65
.Cm set :
the value cannot be encoded as the type, or is invalid
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ moobfs-attr set memory.md kind string decision
.Dl $ moobfs-attr get memory.md kind
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getfattr 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-check 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-index 1 ,
.Xr setfattr 1
.Pp
docs/tools.md and docs/spec-m2.md in the MoobFS repository,
.Lk https://github.com/studiomoob/llmoobfs
